# Rule Length Limitation

## Context
- When creating or updating any Cursor rule files
- When rules begin to grow in complexity
- When rules cover multiple related concerns

## Requirements
- Limit all rule files to a maximum of 200 lines
- Break complex rules into multiple focused rules if they exceed the limit
- Ensure examples are concise and directly illustrate the rule
- Remove redundant content or verbose explanations
- Maintain high information density while respecting the line limit

## Examples

<example>
```markdown
---
description: Format code consistently to improve readability
globs: **/*.{js,ts}
---

# Code Formatting

## Context
- When writing or modifying source code
- When establishing project conventions

## Requirements
- Use consistent indentation (2 spaces)
- Limit line length to 80 characters
- Use semicolons consistently
- Place opening braces on the same line

